Package: enforcer-mcp
Section: net
Priority: optional
Architecture: all
Maintainer: enforcer-swarm <enforcer@localhost>
Depends: python3 (>= 3.11), python3-venv, python3-pip, adduser, systemd, ca-certificates
Recommends: aircrack-ng, iw, wireless-tools
Description: Enforcer MCP server for distributed wireless pentesting swarms
 The enforcer-mcp service exposes a Model Context Protocol (MCP) endpoint
 over HTTP+SSE so autonomous LLM agents (Hermes, Claude, etc.) can drive
 offensive wireless tools — airodump-ng, wifite, aireplay-ng — across a
 mesh of swarm nodes.
 .
 Designed to run on small ARM/x86 nodes (Raspberry Pi, mini PCs, spare
 laptops) connected via Tailscale to a central cockpit (the enforcer
 Android app). Each node advertises its tool registry and audit log
 over its own bearer-token-secured MCP transport.
 .
 Features include real PTY-backed sessions for interactive curses tools,
 a bounded SQLite audit log, and a YAML-driven tool registry that can
 be live-synced from the cockpit.
